NAME
    mkdir - create one or more directories

SYNOPSIS
    mkdir DIR [DIR...]

DESCRIPTION
    Creates each DIR. The parent directory must already exist — there
    is no -p flag. If DIR already exists (whether as a file or a
    directory), mkdir fails for that name.

EXAMPLES
    mkdir tmp
    mkdir /var/log /var/spool
    mkdir nested/subdir         # fails if nested/ doesn't exist

EXIT STATUS
    0   every DIR was created
    1   at least one DIR could not be created (already exists, parent
        missing, FS full, no permission)

SEE ALSO
    rmdir(1), ls(1)

NOTES
    No -p (create intermediate dirs), no -m (mode). New dirs get
    mode 0755 (rwxr-xr-x) and inherit the caller's uid/gid.
